#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157189 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157369 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "697e5bea-20b4-5de0-9992-7a67ee932809" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Continuous Random Variable Given a Two-Branch PDF"}] :question/id #uuid "0a870e80-5a73-59d2-997f-bec2d9a947e2" :question/math-academy-id "e-7988" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\textrm E[X] = \\dfrac {10}{3},$ compute $\\textrm{Var}[X].$\n![](images/50/50e7428db936f89942d4c775d2dfe7691b853a9ca729e30c1958cb25b6c1e8d2.svg)" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\textrm E [X^2] - \\textrm E[X]^2\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\textrm E[X^2],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}{x}^{2}\\cdot (8-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}(8{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2})|}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{67}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{67}{6}-{(\\frac{10}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157190 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157370 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c834972a-1ed0-585c-803c-906fcea8cea8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Continuous Random Variable Given a Three-Branch PDF"}] :question/id #uuid "77bbf810-ec26-5224-9d3e-62de3e0529fb" :question/math-academy-id "e-7990" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function given below. Given that $\\textrm E[X]\\approx 1.791\\,67,$ compute $\\textrm{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n![](images/f6/f63c459b8c212033b5dbe5f0c3a4176b7f921788bed579e8615d1a3a3d9b3f17.svg)" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\textrm E [X^2] - \\textrm E[X]^2\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\textrm E[X^2]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{3}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{12}|}_{0}^{2}+{(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4})|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & ≈4.041\\,67\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & ≈4.041\\,67-(1.791\\,67)^{2} \\\\  & ≈0.83\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430392 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157369 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "697e5bea-20b4-5de0-9992-7a67ee932809" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Continuous Random Variable Given a Two-Branch PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e83b986-ddee-59b4-802a-948fde980775" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430365} {:answer/id #uuid "2fc2ed58-b9d2-5a83-88bb-b53d2ba1ebbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430368} {:answer/id #uuid "46c1ec12-647f-5e2e-bec8-78411670d8a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430371} {:answer/id #uuid "6d0d07f3-021e-5286-b989-c71ed8afa664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430377} {:answer/id #uuid "978f294f-61d3-5b38-8c43-23fb7ae51bcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430381}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46c1ec12-647f-5e2e-bec8-78411670d8a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430371} :answer-field/id #uuid "922f5d01-e962-51be-9d91-e5c9f7c8303a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430388}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6332f216-e713-5bbb-8f9f-dbf095406d20" :question/math-academy-id "q-131167" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{6}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{x}{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}|}_{0}^{6} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{6}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{6}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{18}|}_{0}^{6} \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =12-{(3)}^{2} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430390 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157370 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c834972a-1ed0-585c-803c-906fcea8cea8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Continuous Random Variable Given a Three-Branch PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1204147e-9d6e-5e43-8474-be634d7db4f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430366} {:answer/id #uuid "1efa5566-7842-5b7d-abc6-3035b571fbef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430367} {:answer/id #uuid "4b1cc392-4060-5a10-aaea-a16a825992de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430373} {:answer/id #uuid "635dd8c1-f102-56ce-a2d5-2b936e82ad9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{72}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430376} {:answer/id #uuid "ee6aa4d5-c7a1-5ab9-8654-14774348fc7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "635dd8c1-f102-56ce-a2d5-2b936e82ad9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{72}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430376} :answer-field/id #uuid "03117e06-c0a6-56f8-b0fb-52f9c75a1cf1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430385}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "572f0ee2-d90d-5ec7-a063-65cce5fd61fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-131262" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{5}{6},$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x}{2}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{8}|}_{0}^{1}+(-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}){|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}-{(\\frac{5}{6})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{72}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430391 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157370 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c834972a-1ed0-585c-803c-906fcea8cea8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Continuous Random Variable Given a Three-Branch PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "441dd7e3-e030-5310-9ecb-7b67a3982bac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.98" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430370} {:answer/id #uuid "4f0b7271-9bb4-550c-b029-e79bed346a53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430374} {:answer/id #uuid "81542d0a-0fb0-50ab-9035-5794eba4e936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.43" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430380} {:answer/id #uuid "c9be22c8-e40d-5cc8-8a81-8a499de04f94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430382} {:answer/id #uuid "e9cd7562-368d-5fd1-be77-af5eda236982" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f0b7271-9bb4-550c-b029-e79bed346a53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430374} :answer-field/id #uuid "49546c79-a4c5-5d04-8800-05585ba7aeb8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430386}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5874ecb6-66d6-5729-9147-ef1e0e5bab53" :question/math-academy-id "q-90539" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{17}{24},$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}, & 0<x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}, & 1\\le x, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}|}_{0}^{1}+{(-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}-{(\\frac{17}{24})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{143}{576} \\\\  & ≈0.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430389 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157369 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "697e5bea-20b4-5de0-9992-7a67ee932809" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Continuous Random Variable Given a Two-Branch PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31e8a360-bbb6-5ff2-b1db-6f35ee0fb9fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.66" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430369} {:answer/id #uuid "497c8e24-3ed3-5e00-ac42-19805589f75b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430372} {:answer/id #uuid "5f1cc211-5e0d-51fa-be2e-fd25ee32fb31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.78" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430375} {:answer/id #uuid "715e9c36-f6d8-592b-8bb2-6d5a3d196969" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430378} {:answer/id #uuid "76363301-ac77-5722-bc0a-5eb853e83c26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31e8a360-bbb6-5ff2-b1db-6f35ee0fb9fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.66" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430369} :answer-field/id #uuid "83b0e856-ac3a-5380-970b-faca3f779b77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "30cb3fc9-0bbc-51d2-bbe4-e74999cc9efd" :question/math-academy-id "q-90562" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2x}{15},\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}x\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2x}{15})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(\\frac{2x}{3}-\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{15})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{45})|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2x}{15})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{15})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{30})|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{2}-{(\\frac{11}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{33}{50} \\\\  & =0.66.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
